# Build context exclusions.
#
# Both images (Dockerfile = broker, proxy/Dockerfile = proxy) build from
# the REPO ROOT, so everything not excluded here is uploaded to the daemon on
# every build. Patterns without `**/` match only at the context root — that is
# why the nested target/ and node_modules/ dirs need the recursive form.

# Dependencies — reinstalled inside the image with `npm ci`
**/node_modules

# Rust build artifacts — ~12 GB locally, rebuilt inside the image
**/target

# Frontend build output — regenerated by the frontend stages
app/dist
server/webapp/dist
proxy/console/dist
# ...except the committed one, which server/Dockerfile copies verbatim: the
# slim test image has no frontend stage to regenerate it from.
!server/webapp/dist

# Python virtualenvs — 280 MB of client-py/.venv would otherwise be uploaded to
# the daemon on every build, and no Dockerfile copies it.
**/.venv

# Legacy / non-Rust build artifacts
server/build/
server/bin/
server/vendor/

# Benchmarks, docs tooling and generated sites: never copied by any Dockerfile
benchmark-queen/
webdoc/
docs/
assets/
examples/
helm/
helm_queen/
test/

# Local dev cell state (pids, logs, spool)
proxy/.devcell/
proxy/queen-proxy-spool/

# Git
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Documentation
*.md
!README.md

# IDE and editor files
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log
logs/

# Test files
src/test/
test-*.js
debug-*.js

# Other
.env
.env.*
*.zip
*.tar.gz
